                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 26 at 3:48AM HST until September 26 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "Hurricane Nolo remains nearly stationary south of the Big Island.\nThe possibility of heavy rain could lead to localized flooding over\nportions of the Big Island and Maui.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Big Island, Maui, Lanai, Molokai, and Kahoolawe.\n\n* WHEN...Through this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flood prone roads and other low lying areas may be closed\ndue to elevated runoff and overflowing streams. Urban areas may\nreceive more significant flooding and property damage due to rapid\nrunoff. Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of\nstreams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along\nwith property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.\nLandslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The possibility remains for localized flooding over areas of the\nBig Island and Maui due to heavy rain from slow moving Hurricane\nNolo to the south of the Big Island. Areas most at risk for\nflooding are the windward and southeast portions of the Big\nIsland where the ground remains saturated after recent rains.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
